{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-70889",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The derivative of the natural logarithm is the reciprocal function:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x}\n$$\n\nWe apply our formula and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6e\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =6e\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =6e\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{6e}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
